  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CUBES: A pathway to enabling Brazilian leadership in ground-based astronomy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term sustainable growth in Brazil requires increased capability for innovation in high-tech sectors, but recent economic challenges are threatening investment in scientific research. This proposal will enhance the science base in Brazil in a research area where it is well positioned for international leadership if given the right support and resources,   Astronomy is one of the most accessible areas of contemporary scientific research. Here we propose UK support of Brazil&apos;s ambition to develop a world-leading instrument (&apos;CUBES&apos;) for the European Southern Observatory (ESO). The proposed activities will help build Brazilian science capacity and upskill its engineers. They will help Brazil improve its scientific and industrial return in astronomy, in support of its economic development. They will also position Brazilian engineers and researchers to lead future international projects, from which they can act as mentors to inspire the next generation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
